\import{spin-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\taxon{Example}
\title{semidirect products make Clifford theory concrete}
\tag{math}
\tag{fgap}
\tag{group-algebra}
\tag{representation}

\p{Suppose #{G=N\rtimes H}. Conjugation by #{H} permutes the irreducible
constituents of #{V|_N}. Their stabilizers are the inertia subgroups, so the
orbit and homogeneity statements in [[fgap-001P]] and [[fgap-001Q]] reduce
the search for irreducible #{G}-representations to stabilizer data,
projective extension, and induction. This is why Clifford theory is the
standard character-theoretic route for semidirect products.}

\p{For the current finite example, #{Q_8\rtimes C_3\cong 2T}. The action and
ordinary skew-Group-Algebra realization are recorded in [[fgap-0015]] and
[[fgap-001E]]. They supply the normal-subgroup and algebraic input to this
route, but they do not yet give the full character table of #{2T}. The same
distinction separates the completed infrastructure from the remaining
representation-theoretic calculation.}
